Phase 7 + 8 — Premium Editor Layout & Content-Type Sidebar Icons

WHAT:
- NotesBlockEditor.module.css: added solid #000000 background to hide dotted canvas grid
- NotesBlockEditor.module.css: applied max-width 800px centered layout (Notion-style)
- WorkspaceSection.tsx: replaced hardcoded <FileText> icon with conditional render:
    canvas -> SquarePen, kanban -> Layout, markdown -> FileText
- RecentlyClosedSection.tsx: same conditional icon logic as above
- useRecentlyClosedNotes.ts: added contentType field to RecentlyClosedNote interface
- NotesSidebar.tsx: passes selectedNote.contentType into useRecentlyClosedNotes hook

WHY:
The sidebar showed FileText for every note regardless of type, making it impossible
to visually distinguish canvas/kanban/markdown notes at a glance. The block editor
was rendered inside the canvas container (.workspace) which has a radial dot-grid
background — applying a solid black bg to the editor container masks this.

FILES: NotesBlockEditor.module.css, NotesBlockEditor.tsx, WorkspaceSection.tsx,
       RecentlyClosedSection.tsx, useRecentlyClosedNotes.ts, NotesSidebar.tsx
